.TH SCRIPTS 1 "October 2026" "scripts" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
scripts \- unified manager for the nada.mu personal utilities ecosystem
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scripts
[\fBcommand\fR] [\fBoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBscripts\fR manages the installation, updates, and removal of personal administration, workstation, and cryptographic utilities.
It supports both local development workflows and standalone remote installations.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B update
Synchronizes and updates all utilities with the repository. Verifies SHA-256 digests, installs missing scripts, updates modified files, installs man pages and shell completions, and removes deprecated utilities. If executed within a git repository, automatically pulls the latest changes. (Aliases: \fBsync\fR, \fBinstall\fR).
.TP
.B list
Lists all utilities declared in the manifest, showing their installation status and paths.
.TP
.B doctor \fR[\fB\-\-fix\fR]
Performs a comprehensive diagnostic health check of the system environment, core runtime dependencies (\fBbash\fR, \fBgit\fR, \fBsystemd\fR, \fBuv\fR), optional feature packages (\fBrclone\fR, \fBopenrgb\fR, \fBlibnotify\fR, \fBbtrfs-progs\fR, \fBblueman\fR), PATH variables, and shell completions. On Arch Linux and CachyOS, provides exact \fBpacman\fR package remediation commands. Passing \fB\-\-fix\fR automatically attempts installation of missing dependencies.
.TP
.B pkgbuild \fR[\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-install\fR] [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-clean\fR] [\fB\-\-local\fR|\fB\-\-remote\fR] [\fB\-\-printsrcinfo\fR]
Builds a native Arch Linux / CachyOS package (\fB.pkg.tar.zst\fR) via \fBmakepkg\fR. By default, packages the local repository state directly without needing to clone from git remote. Use \fB\-\-install\fR to automatically install the built package with \fBpacman \-U\fR. Use \fB\-\-printsrcinfo\fR to generate \fB.SRCINFO\fR for AUR submissions.
.TP
.B nautilus \fR[\fIinstall\fR|\fIsync\fR|\fIlist\fR|\fIuninstall\fR]
Manages GNOME Files (Nautilus) context menu integration scripts for rapid file uploads, bidirectional syncing, and Bluetooth transfers.
.TP
.B autoupdate \fR[\fIstatus\fR|\fIenable\fR|\fIdisable\fR] [\fItarget\fR]
Manage automated updates across multiple mechanisms: systemd timers (user and system scope), interactive shell startup hooks (~/.bashrc, ~/.zshrc, ~/.config/fish/config.fish), cron jobs (crontab, /etc/cron.daily), APT hooks (/etc/apt/apt.conf.d/99scripts), Pacman hooks (/etc/pacman.d/hooks/99scripts.hook), and git post-merge hooks. Supported targets: \fBsystemd\fR, \fBshell\fR, \fBcron\fR, \fBapt\fR, \fBpacman\fR, \fBgit\fR, \fBall\fR.
.TP
.B prune
Scans for and removes deprecated or orphaned utilities, man pages, and shell completions. (Alias: \fBclean\fR).
.TP
.B uninstall \fR[\fIutility...\fR]
Removes installed utilities, man pages, and shell completions. If specific utility names are supplied, removes only the designated utilities and their associated assets. If omitted, prompts to remove all managed utilities.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-scope " " \fIuser\fR|\fIsystem\fR
Target directory scope: \fBuser\fR for \fB~/.local/bin\fR or \fBsystem\fR for \fB/usr/local/bin\fR. If omitted, automatically determined by existing installations and user privileges.
.TP
.BR \-\-category " " \fIall\fR|\fIserver\fR|\fIdesktop\fR|\fImedia\fR
Filter which categories of scripts to install (defaults to \fBall\fR).
.TP
.BR \-\-method " " \fIlink\fR|\fIcopy\fR
Installation method: symlink (default for git repository) or copy (default for standalone).
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-pull
Skip pulling changes from git remote when updating inside a local git repository clone.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Run non-interactively, accepting all defaults.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help synopsis.
